            <ArticleTitle>Ureteroenteric Fistula Revealed by 99mTc-DTPA Renal Scan.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>807-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1097/RLU.0000000000001320</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 55-year-old woman with a history of cervical carcinoma, status post hysterectomy and radiation therapy 8 years prior, presented worsening back pain for 9 months. The patient underwent a Tc-DTPA renal scan, which showed that a vertically linear tracer distribution was seen alongside the right ureter. Ureteroenteric fistula was confirmed and repaired by surgery.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
